<title>RUSSIA: Russian 364-day T-bill yields 18.84 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 364-day T-bill yields 18.84 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of Russian 364-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 18.84 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had expected the yield to be between 18.72-18.93 percent.</p>
<p>The series 21080 bills, maturing on July 22, 1998, the closest maturity date to the new issue, closed on Tuesday at 84.45 to yield 18.77 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number		  21082</p>
<p>    Issue volume		   6.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		  1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		 6.88 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)		    5.76 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Sold			     4.70 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Proceeds			 3.95 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Average yield		  18.84 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield     18.90 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		  84.18 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	84.14 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			    364 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		  July 29, 1998</p>
<p>On July 30, the Finance Ministry will offer four trillion roubles in 182-day T-bills (series 21081).</p>
<p>It will also repay about 6.72 trillion roubles ($1.2 billion) in a maturing 259-day T-bill (series 22058).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520 ($ = 5807 Russian Roubles)</p>
